# DUSKLING: the first rooms stay gentle (the player feedback of 30/09). A
# steady player stands at a spot, waits, walks on and jumps when its front
# is some distance from the stop ahead, holding the tap some frames; every
# mix of wait, distance (-10 to 30 px) and hold (0 to 16 frames) is played
# (cheat window, see dk_window). Every obstacle of rooms 0-6, spot to spot
# along the way on, must let enough of those inputs through:
#   rooms 0-2: 50% of all inputs, 50% at the worst moment (no timing),
#              and 10 of the 17 holds at the best take-off (no precise hop)
#   rooms 3-6: 25% of all inputs, and a way through at half the moments
# cheat window ROOM X Y EDGE GOAL_X0 GOAL_X1 GOAL_FEET PERIOD WAIT_STEP [SLAM]
# (px; a goal x0 of -1 is the way out; SLAM: it slams from pink ledges)
game duskling
wait 5
# room 0
# the walk to the pit
cheat window 0 11 141 -1 -1 9 0 150 50 0
expect win_pct >= 50
expect win_worst >= 50
expect win_hw >= 10
# room 1
# bump
cheat window 1 11 141 -1 180 239 150 150 50 0
expect win_pct >= 50
expect win_worst >= 50
expect win_hw >= 10
# step up 2
cheat window 1 191 141 -1 240 339 130 150 50 0
